\id PSA 20-PSA-web.sfm World English Bible (WEB) - abridged test fixture
\h Psalms
\toc2 Psalms
\mt1 The Psalms
\cl Psalm
\c 1
\ms1 BOOK 1
\q1
\v 1 Blessed is the man who doesn’t walk in the counsel of the wicked,
\q2 nor stand on the path of sinners,
\q2 nor sit in the seat of scoffers;
\q1
\v 2 but his delight is in \nd Yahweh\nd*’s law.
\q2 On his law he meditates day and night.
\q1
\v 3 He will be like a tree planted by the streams of water,
\q2 that produces its fruit in its season.
\q1
\v 4 The wicked are not so,
\q2 but are like the chaff which the wind drives away.
\q1
\v 5 Therefore the wicked shall not stand in the judgment,
\q1
\v 6 For \nd Yahweh\nd* knows the way of the righteous,
\q2 but the way of the wicked shall perish.
\c 2
\q1
\v 1 Why do the nations rage,
\q2 and the peoples plot a vain thing?
\q1
\v 2 The kings of the earth take a stand, and the rulers take counsel together.
\c 3
\d A Psalm by David, when he fled from Absalom his son.
\q1
\v 1 \nd Yahweh\nd*, how my adversaries have increased!
\q1
\v 2 Many there are who say of my soul,
\q2 “There is no help for him in God.” \qs Selah.\qs*
\b
\q1
\v 3 But you, \nd Yahweh\nd*, are a shield around me,
\q1
\v 4 I cry to \nd Yahweh\nd* with my voice,
\q2 and he answers me out of his holy mountain. \qs Selah.\qs*
\b
\q1
\v 5 I laid myself down and slept.
\q1
\v 6 I will not be afraid of tens of thousands of people
\q1
\v 7 Arise, \nd Yahweh\nd*! Save me, my God!
\q1
\v 8 Salvation belongs to \nd Yahweh\nd*.
\q2 May your blessing be on your people. \qs Selah.\qs*
\c 23
\d A Psalm by David.
\q1
\v 1 \nd Yahweh\nd* is my shepherd;
\q2 I shall lack nothing.
\q1
\v 2 He makes me lie down in green pastures.
\q2 He leads me beside still waters.
\q1
\v 3 He restores my soul.
\q1
\v 4 Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,
\q2 I will fear no evil, for you are with me.
\q1
\v 5 You prepare a table before me in the presence of my enemies.
\q1
\v 6 Surely goodness and loving kindness shall follow me all the days of my life.
